var ubuntuValue171 = "When curl &lt; 7.84.0 does FTP transfers secured by krb5, it handles message verification failures wrongly. This flaw makes it possible for a Man-In-The-Middle attack to go unnoticed and even allows it to inject data to the client.  Update Instructions:  Run `sudo pro fix CVE-2022-32208` to fix the vulnerability. The problem can be corrected by updating your system to the following package versions:  curl - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.12 libcurl3-gnutls - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.12 libcurl3-nss - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.12 libcurl4 - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.12 No subscription required"

