var ubuntuValue240 = "When asked to both use a `.netrc` file for credentials and to follow HTTP redirects, curl could leak the password used for the first host to the followed-to host under certain circumstances. This flaw only manifests itself if the netrc file has an entry that matches the redirect target hostname but the entry either omits just the password or omits both login and password.  Update Instructions:  Run `sudo pro fix CVE-2024-11053` to fix the vulnerability. The problem can be corrected by updating your system to the following package versions:  curl - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25 libcurl3-gnutls - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25 libcurl3-nss - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25 libcurl4 - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25 No subscription required"

