var ubuntuValue305 = "libcurl would reuse a previously created connection even when some mTLS config related option had been changed that should have prohibited reuse. libcurl keeps previously used connections in a connection pool for subsequent transfers to reuse if one of them matches the setup. However, some TLS settings related to client certificates were left out from the configuration match checks, making them match too easily. In particular options related to the private key.  Update Instructions:  Run `sudo pro fix CVE-2026-8932` to fix the vulnerability. The problem can be corrected by updating your system to the following package versions:  curl - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25+esm7 libcurl3-gnutls - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25+esm7 libcurl3-nss - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25+esm7 libcurl4 - 7.68.0-1ubuntu2.25+esm7 Available with Ubuntu Pro (Infra-only): https://ubuntu.com/pro"

